course: dictionary
lesson: 15028
title: Restoration: mending and bringing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Restoration means repairing something old or damaged so it looks or works as it did before. Think of an old clock that is mended until it ticks again.
explain: Restoration can also mean bringing something back, like power, peace or health. «Power came back after the restoration of the electricity lines.» The power had gone off, and now it is on again.
explain: A restoration can also be the thing that has been repaired. «The painting in the hall is a restoration of a picture painted 300 years ago.» To check your meaning, swap in «repair» or «bringing back». If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Restoration is a noun, so it names an action or a thing: restoration, restorations.
fact: Restoration means repairing something old or damaged so it looks or works as it did before.
fact: «Restoration» can also mean bringing something back, such as «restoration of power» or «restoration of peace».
fact: In science, «habitat restoration» means bringing nature back to a place, such as planting trees so wildlife can return.
fact: «Under restoration» means being repaired right now, and «restoration work» is the job of repairing.
exercise: «The museum is showing the restoration of an old ship.» What does restoration mean here? | Painting over the ship to hide it | *Repairing the ship so it looks as it did before | Selling the ship to a new owner
exercise: «Power came back after the restoration of the electricity lines.» What does restoration mean here? | Cutting the lines down | Moving the lines to a new town | *Bringing the power back on
exercise: Mia says, «The old chair is under restoration.» What does under restoration mean? | *Being repaired right now | Being thrown away | Being sold at a market | Being painted for a party
test: «The workers spent three years on the restoration of the old church.» What is the restoration work? | Knocking the church down | Counting the people who visit it | Building a brand new church next to the old one | *Repairing the old church so it looks as it did before
test: Which of these is a restoration? | A pile of bricks in a field | *A painting that has been carefully repaired so it looks as it did long ago | A plan for a new house
exam: «After the flood, the restoration of the town's clean water took a week.» What does restoration mean here? | Making the water dirty | Measuring how much water fell | *Bringing the clean water back | Drinking the water quickly
